Microsoft scores CVE-2020-17103 CVSS 3.1 7.0, not 7.8, and re-released it on 2026-06-09 with the June 2026 Windows updates as the fix for MiniPlasma, so the flaw is patched rather than unpatched. BleepingComputer tested the exploit itself on Windows 11 Pro with the May 2026 updates, and Will Dormann separately confirmed it on the latest public Windows 11. MiniPlasma follows BlueHammer, RedSun, UnDefend, YellowKey and GreenPlasma in the researcher's 2026 series rather than being its third proof of concept, and the monitoring advice is ThreatLocker's two registry paths.
